<script>
import { url } from '@abide/abide'
import layoutSpecSource from 'crm/e2e/Layout.test.ts' with { type: 'text' }
import errorPageSource from 'crm/src/companies/error.abide' with { type: 'text' }
import errorPageTestSource from 'crm/src/companies/ErrorPage.test.ts' with { type: 'text' }
import getCompanySource from 'crm/src/companies/getCompany.handler.ts' with { type: 'text' }
import layoutSource from 'crm/src/companies/layout.abide' with { type: 'text' }
import layoutTestSource from 'crm/src/companies/Layout.test.ts' with { type: 'text' }
import CompaniesFrame from 'crm/src/companies/lib/CompaniesFrame.abide'
import companiesFrameSource from 'crm/src/companies/lib/CompaniesFrame.abide' with { type: 'text' }
import MissingCompany from 'crm/src/companies/lib/MissingCompany.abide'
import missingCompanySource from 'crm/src/companies/lib/MissingCompany.abide' with { type: 'text' }

import Doc from '#src/lib/Doc.abide'
import Example from '#src/lib/Example.abide'
import Registry from '#src/lib/Registry.abide'
import Section from '#src/lib/Section.abide'
</script>

<Doc>
    <Section title="A file's path is the address it answers">
        <p>A file's path below <code>src</code> is its address. Nothing else names a route.</p>

        <table>
            <thead><tr><th>File</th><th>Answers on</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr><td><code>src/index.abide</code></td><td><code>/</code></td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>src/contacts/index.abide</code></td><td><code>/contacts</code></td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>src/contacts/listContacts.handler.ts</code></td><td><code>GET /contacts/listContacts</code>, the handler its default export declares</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>src/contacts/lib/ContactList.abide</code></td><td>no address: a component the pages import</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>src/contacts/lib/ContactList.test.ts</code></td><td>no address: what <code>bun test</code> runs</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>

        <p>Code that is not an address goes in a directory that never is, and a file's name
            decides where it runs:</p>

        <table>
            <thead><tr><th>Path</th><th>What goes in it</th><th>Where it runs</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr><td><code>src/**</code></td><td>the app</td><td>both sides, unless its name says otherwise</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>src/**/</code></td><td>pages, layouts and handler files, routed by their path</td><td>a page on both sides; a handler on the server, with a call in its place in the browser</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>**/lib/**</code></td><td>components and modules</td><td>wherever they are imported</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>**/lib/**/&lt;name&gt;.server.&lt;extension&gt;</code></td><td>the database, secrets, anything the browser never loads</td><td>the server alone; a page importing it is a compile error</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>**/&lt;name&gt;.test.ts</code></td><td>tests, beside what they test</td><td><code>bun test</code>, never served</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>**/&lt;name&gt;.bench.ts</code></td><td>benches, beside what they time</td><td><code>bun run bench</code>, never served</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>**/&lt;NAME&gt;.param.ts</code></td><td>what a segment named <code>NAME</code> takes. See <a href={url('/pages/pages')}>Pages and layouts</a></td><td>wherever an address is matched</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>**/&lt;name&gt;.d.ts</code></td><td>types, beside what they type</td><td>nowhere; the checker reads them</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>**/public/**</code></td><td>files answered as they are</td><td>nowhere; each is sent at its path</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>

        <p>Any other file beside the pages fails the build, so listing a directory lists its
            routes.</p>
    </Section>

    <Section title="A layout holds what the companies pages share">
        <Example
            id="layout"
            app="crm"
            title="`layout.abide` — the header the companies pages share, built once"
            summary="The companies header holds a note for the call you are on. Type one, then open a company and come back: the page changes, and the note stays."
            files={{
                'src/companies/lib/CompaniesFrame.abide': companiesFrameSource,
                'src/companies/layout.abide': layoutSource,
                'src/companies/Layout.test.ts': layoutTestSource,
                'e2e/Layout.test.ts': layoutSpecSource,
            }}
        >
            <CompaniesFrame />
        </Example>

        <p>A <code>**/layout.abide</code> wraps every page at its directory and below, and
            <code>&lt;slot/&gt;</code> is where the page renders. A navigation between two of its pages
            swaps what is in the slot and leaves the layout alone, so its inputs, its scroll and
            anything it was loading stay as they were. Layouts nest: the root layout wraps this one.</p>

        <p>A layout's <code>&lt;script server&gt;</code> files hooks for the same pages. The
            companies layout files its <code>onError</code> hook there.</p>

        <p>A package can ship pages too. <code>import '…' with &#123; type: 'routes' &#125;</code>
            in a file of your app serves every page and handler in the named directory below that
            file's directory, and moving the line moves them.</p>
    </Section>

    <Section title="`error.abide` answers when a page cannot">
        <Example
            id="error-page"
            app="crm"
            title="`error.abide` — a company that is not there"
            summary="An old link points at a company that was merged away. The handler refuses at once, and the companies error page answers with a 404."
            files={{
                'src/companies/lib/MissingCompany.abide': missingCompanySource,
                'src/companies/error.abide': errorPageSource,
                'src/companies/getCompany.handler.ts': getCompanySource,
                'src/companies/ErrorPage.test.ts': errorPageTestSource,
            }}
        >
            <MissingCompany />
        </Example>

        <p>An <code>**/error.abide</code> is found the way a layout is: the nearest one above the
            page that failed. It gets the refusal as <code>failure</code>, and each refusal's
            <code>is</code> narrows it. An address no page answers is <code>refuse.notFound</code> too. A
            page asked with a method other than <code>GET</code> or <code>HEAD</code> is a 405,
            painted by the same page, with <code>allow: GET, HEAD</code> on the answer.</p>

        <p>The refusal has to come in the page's first turn to set the status. That is why
            <code>getCompany</code> refuses before it waits. An error page that fails itself hands
            off to the next one up.</p>

        <p>A request for a page that is neither a navigation nor a <code>fetch</code>, such as an
            <code>&lt;img&gt;</code> pointed at <code>/companies/initech</code>, gets a 404 with no
            body, and the page is never set up for it.</p>
    </Section>

    <Registry />
</Doc>
